+--------------------------+
| Release of autozmat 1.83 |
+--------------------------+

Changes from the previous version
----------------------------------

1. Atomtyping is performed on domain by domain basis.
   This saves time and yields a better atomtyping.
   For a domain with more than 500 atoms, atomtyping will
   not be tried because it may cause a system crash due to
   a heavy memory consumption.

2. Z-matrix can be written in PEPZ format.

3. Mindtool format can retain chain and residue information
   as well as charge, sigma, epsilon, and atom name.

4. Sample data files for each format were added in 'sample' directory.
   Now testing the program can be performed easily just by typing
   'make test'.

5. '-g' (general) option was added. Options may be combined using ','
delimiter.
   E.g., -g verbose,remove_dummy

   -g verbose        (same as -V)
   -g remove_dummy   (same as -x)
   -g no_atomtyping  (same as -a)
   -g break_mind     (In mindtool format, '%' is treated as molecule
separator,
                      rather than a residue separator)
   -g pepz=number    (specifies a starting atom type in PEPZ format. E.g.,
                      -g pepz=500)

6. Option '-z default' is equivalent to
 '-z varbond,addbond,varangle,auto_addangle,vardihed_explicit,auto_adddihed'.
   'vardihed_explicit' gives a list of all variable dihedrals with
   explicit torsion types. 'vardihed' results in merely a range of atom
   centers, e.g., 6-12.
   In this case, torsion typing will be done inside BOSS.

   So, if you want to leave torsion typing to BOSS, use
   '-z varbond,addbond,varangle,auto_addangle,vardihed,auto_adddihed' for
   fully flexible molecules. This is equivalent to
   '-z default,~vardihed_explicit,vardihed'.
   (The '~' sign negates an option.)

7. Numberous bug fixes and enhancements.
   I can't list them all here. I think this version is much more stable
than 1.82.

Availability
-------------

Source code and binaries for a few operating systems are available
from ~lim/autozmat directory on doctor.
Get 'autozmat1.83_atomtype.tar.gz' for a version with atomtyping
and 'autozmat1.83_noatomtype.tar.gz' for one without atomtyping.
For compilation and installation, read 00README file in the distribution.
Impatient people would want to do just
        make clean_installed
        make
        make test
        make install

Of course, patient people should read 00README file first.

